PCP atop and standalone atop coexistence

Use `pcp atop` and `pcp atopsar`. Manuals: pcp-atop(1), pcp-atopsar(1),
and pcp-atoprc(5). PCP no longer installs plain atop/atopsar aliases.

PCP recording units:
  pcp-atop.service          continuous PCP archive recording
  pcp-atop-daily.timer      daily rotation schedule
  pcp-atop-daily.service    restarts pcp-atop.service for daily rotation

The timer implicitly selects pcp-atop-daily.service. The recording service
binds to and enables the timer through BindsTo= and Also=.
Configuration remains /etc/pcp/sysconfig/atop. Archives default to
/var/log/pcp/pmimport/atop. The maintenance helper remains
/usr/libexec/pcp/bin/atop-daily; see atop-daily(1).

Interactive PCP defaults are /etc/pcp/atoprc and ~/.pcp-atoprc. Previously
PCP read /etc/atoprc and ~/.atoprc, shared with standalone atop.
Copy only settings intended for PCP into the new files.

Before upgrading, if the old atop.service runs the PCP implementation,
stop and disable that service and its atop-daily.timer. After upgrading,
enable/start pcp-atop.service if PCP recording is wanted. Do not blindly
disable atop.service after installing standalone atop: it is then atop's
service. Recording configuration needs no move. PCP import recordings now default
to /var/log/pcp/pmimport (previously /var/log). To keep existing PCP atop
recordings in place, explicitly set LOGPATH in /etc/pcp/sysconfig/atop;
otherwise move only PCP archives into /var/log/pcp/pmimport/atop while
recording is stopped. Do not mix PCP archives with standalone atop logs.
This import-log default also applies to other PCP import tools.
The package does not start, stop, or migrate services automatically.
